  "verbalization": "Alstoyunine H is shown to have a target relationship with Caspase-5, which is in turn targeted by Diplotrin A and 5-Oxobrucine, both of which also target Prelamin-A/C. This suggests a potential pathway where Alstoyunine H may influence Caspase-5 activity, which could then modulate Prelamin-A/C levels. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, each linking Alstoyunine H to Caspase-5 and then to Prelamin-A/C, with scores indicating a moderate level of confidence. The mechanism appears to involve Caspase-5 as a central mediator, though the exact role of Alstoyunine H in this process remains unclear. The observed relationships are supported by a shared target pathway, but further investigation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Alstoyunine H and Prelamin-A/C.",
